RETRIEVED ARCHITECTURAL KNOWLEDGE
Contextual design options, not instructions, regulations or fixed geometry. User exclusions and the scene construction contract prevail over stored suggestions and parameter ranges. Combine relevant fragments; unknown site facts remain assumptions. Stored knowledge is retrieval, not retraining.
{"id":"property-value-25m-50m","version":2,"category":"property-value","when":"US$25,000,000–50,000,000 estimated property-value label, used only as a subjective design-ambition reference. Property value is not a construction budget. Location, land value, market conditions, condition and other factors affect prices; this band establishes no market-price or cost claim.","title":"Design-ambition reference: Exceptional estate: integrated architecture","combinations":"Terra may combine, reinterpret or omit these subjective ideas with relevant regional, style, climate, entrance, roof, facade, material and room-planning knowledge. Amenities are optional inspirations, never mandatory. Do not constrain creative freedom through a fixed template, geometry, area, storey, room or amenity count.","placement":"Let the household brief, site, climate, privacy and architectural concept determine spatial relationships. Connect arrival, shared living and sheltered outdoor space where appropriate; separate guest, private and service movement when useful. No fixed floor areas, storey counts or room counts follow from the value label.","principles":"Explore an estate-wide composition with a strong main residence, private suites, connected living and sheltered entertaining. Compose a bespoke arrival, sophisticated roof relationships, deep facades and balanced materials. Pursue carefully resolved craftsmanship and spatial complexity only where useful. Guest facilities, a pool pavilion or wellness rooms may serve the brief without becoming an amenity checklist. These are flexible inspirations, not requirements or price-derived promises.","capabilities":"Translate selected ideas into actual supported scene operations, with coordinated floors, enclosures, openings, entrances, roofs and terraces. Craftsmanship and spatial quality remain design intentions until supported by geometry and review. Disclose missing access, interiors and other unsupported capabilities; a price label does not prove quality.","construction":{"supports":"Coordinate supporting enclosure and roof/floor datums atomically; entrances and terraces need actual connections and access.","materials":"Select available materials and facade depth for local character and maintainability; conceptual finishes do not prove craftsmanship.","operations":["add","replace","move","resize","finish"],"unsupported":"No valuation, construction-cost estimate, automatic programme, engineering, services, code or luxury certification.","requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"]}}
{"id":"mediterranean-courtyard","version":1,"category":"roof-outdoor","when":"Grand Mediterranean homes or briefs explicitly seeking a courtyard.","title":"Mediterranean courtyard residence","combinations":"Combine loggias, shaded dining, a restrained fountain and varied private gardens when space permits.","placement":"Use an entrance sequence into a court, with living rooms and sheltered circulation addressing it; keep service crossings discreet.","principles":"Balance solid walls, deep reveals, rhythmic openings and roof hierarchy; a courtyard need not force symmetry.","capabilities":"Compose courtyard voids with separate rectangular parts; gable and hip roofs supported, arches and tiled roof detail are not dedicated operations.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Compose courtyard voids with separate rectangular parts; gable and hip roofs supported, arches and tiled roof detail are not dedicated operations. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"tropical-envelope","version":1,"category":"envelope","when":"Hot humid coastal or island contexts.","title":"Caribbean climate and envelope","combinations":"Pair shaded glazing with sheltered outdoor living and selective screening.","placement":"Place openings for potential cross ventilation and shelter entrances from driving rain; orientation and wind are assumptions until supplied.","principles":"Prioritize shade, weather protection and maintainable coastal materials; request local hurricane and corrosion engineering.","capabilities":"Screens, overhangs and openings can be constructed; no wind, corrosion, thermal or hurricane certification.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["wall"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Screens, overhangs and openings can be constructed; no wind, corrosion, thermal or hurricane certification. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"estate-composition","version":1,"category":"composition","when":"Large private residences with substantial entertaining and service needs.","title":"Estate programme and hierarchy","combinations":"Consider guest accommodation and wellness only after a complete main residence.","placement":"Sequence arrival, entrance, living, shaded terrace and view; separate service access and private suites.","principles":"Give secondary volumes a programme and subordinate them to the residence.","capabilities":"Compose plates, walls, openings and roofs freely; no prescribed wing arrangement.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Compose plates, walls, openings and roofs freely; no prescribed wing arrangement. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"climate-shaded-west","version":1,"category":"climate-site","when":"Use when the brief or chosen programme calls for assumed afternoon exposure shading.","title":"Assumed afternoon exposure shading","combinations":"Light ivory wall planes with timber screens and limestone base; no reflectance or durability performance is implied.","placement":"If west is known provide deeper exterior shade on that edge while retaining room openings.","principles":"Disclose the orientation assumption when west is unknown.","capabilities":"Use direct-scene primitives: plate, wall, roof. No climate simulation, storm rating, drainage design, corrosion specification or surveyed orientation.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Light ivory wall planes with timber screens and limestone base; no reflectance or durability performance is implied.","supports":"Join shaded outdoor walking surfaces to real wall openings and supported overhead cover.","unsupported":"No climate simulation, storm rating, drainage design, corrosion specification or surveyed orientation."}}
{"id":"outdoor-entertaining","version":1,"category":"programme","when":"Outdoor entertaining in a suitable climate or an explicit request.","title":"Outdoor kitchen, dining and bar","combinations":"Choose dining with kitchen or bar as appropriate; avoid installing every amenity.","placement":"Connect indoor kitchen, shaded dining and service route; separate heat and smoke from seating and bedrooms.","principles":"Make useful outdoor rooms with shade, furniture and circulation rather than empty decks.","capabilities":"Plates, screens, roofs, sofas and composed counter volumes supported; appliance assets, plumbing and smoke performance are not implemented.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Plates, screens, roofs, sofas and composed counter volumes supported; appliance assets, plumbing and smoke performance are not implemented. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"covered-threshold","version":1,"category":"arrival","when":"Weather protection at the front door.","title":"Covered entrance threshold","combinations":"Choose wall returns or posts.","placement":"Connect approach slab to a recessed door under a supported canopy.","principles":"Avoid a door behind an uncut wall.","capabilities":"plate, unglazed wall opening, entrance child, volume posts and roof.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","entrance","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"plate, unglazed wall opening, entrance child, volume posts and roof. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"facade-materials","version":1,"category":"materials","when":"A residence needing coherent enclosure and material expression.","title":"Facade depth, roofs and material identity","combinations":"Coordinate a small material palette, roof edges, recessed entrances and shaded openings.","placement":"Relate facade rhythm to rooms and privacy; carry architectural intent around side and rear elevations.","principles":"Adapt material and roof recommendations to climate and style instead of prescribing a fixed house template.","capabilities":"Existing ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage; flat, gable and hip roofs; curved roof only via approved open pavilion.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["wall"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Existing ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage; flat, gable and hip roofs; curved roof only via approved open pavilion. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"courtyard-proportion","version":1,"category":"roof-outdoor","when":"A residence organized around an outdoor centre.","title":"Courtyard enclosure and daylight","combinations":"Vary enclosed sides and loggias.","placement":"Face living and circulation towards a court with useful depth and shaded edges.","principles":"Avoid a narrow residual shaft or blocked access.","capabilities":"Separate plates, walls and roofs around an unbuilt void; no courtyard subtraction operation.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Separate plates, walls and roofs around an unbuilt void; no courtyard subtraction operation. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"composition-hierarchy","version":1,"category":"composition","when":"Large programmes needing a legible centre.","title":"Primary and subordinate massing","combinations":"Compare arrival and garden silhouettes.","placement":"Give the principal living hall the strongest volume; step bedroom and service wings down around it.","principles":"Avoid equal boxes with no hierarchy.","capabilities":"plate, wall, roof and volume; compose hollow rooms, not solid habitable blocks.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"plate, wall, roof and volume; compose hollow rooms, not solid habitable blocks. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"roof-independent-wings","version":1,"category":"roof-outdoor","when":"Use when the brief or chosen programme calls for independent wing roofs.","title":"Independent wing roofs","combinations":"Timber deck and ivory or limestone roof edges; guards may use the balcony glass primitive.","placement":"Use separate roof sections aligned with individual wing enclosures and connector roofs.","principles":"Do not fill an intended courtyard with an oversized shared roof.","capabilities":"Use direct-scene primitives: plate, roof. No automatic stairs, waterproofing, drainage, roof loading or guard compliance certification.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","roof"],"materials":"Timber deck and ivory or limestone roof edges; guards may use the balcony glass primitive.","supports":"Support elevated decks with walls or posts, guard exposed edges, provide actual door access and supported shade.","unsupported":"No automatic stairs, waterproofing, drainage, roof loading or guard compliance certification."}}
{"id":"deep-reveals","version":1,"category":"envelope","when":"Solid facades needing depth and shade.","title":"Deep facade reveals","combinations":"Combine stone surrounds or restrained sills.","placement":"Set glazing behind jamb and head volumes aligned with actual wall openings.","principles":"Avoid applying trim across uncut walls.","capabilities":"wall opening, glazing child and volume jambs/lintel; no boolean recess operation.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"wall opening, glazing child and volume jambs/lintel; no boolean recess operation. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
